{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CggKbGSDxHirA2Ux53HFX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is in `money.py` and the test suite passes (4 of 4). I haven't committed or pushed, since you didn't ask me to.\n\n**The bug:** `split_cents` used `total // people` for every share, so the remainder was dropped. `split_cents(100, 3)` returned `[33, 33, 33]`, which sums to 99.\n\n**The fix** (`money.py`): the remainder is now spread one grosz at a time over the first shares.\n\n```python\nshare, remainder = divmod(total, people)\nreturn [share + 1 if i < remainder else share for i in range(people)]\n```\n\n`split_cents(100, 3)` now returns `[34, 33, 33]`. The spot checks all sum to the total: 300/3 gives `[100, 100, 100]`, 0/4 gives zeros, 1/5 gives `[1, 0, 0, 0, 0]`.\n\n**The test:** I added `test_uneven_split_keeps_every_grosz` to `test_money.py` before changing the code. It failed first with `99 != 100`, then passed after the fix. That took about a minute, so the backfill is already done for this case.\n\n**Choices to check before deploy:**\n- The extra grosz goes to the first people in the list. If the bill's ordering matters for who pays it, tell me and I'll change it.\n- Only the `split_cents` behaviour was changed. I didn't touch anything else in `money.py`.\n\n**Still to do:** commit and push when you're ready. The commit will be on `main`, so I'd branch first unless you say otherwise."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":909,"cache_read_input_tokens":22615,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":909},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"51edc9b4-983e-4bc5-8908-dd0efbf6020f","uuid":"01cf0cb3-c453